        "body": "PocketVina 0.3.0 adds the PocketVina Atlas: a database of docking results of drugs against the whole human proteome,\r\ncomputed in advance with PocketVina. You can now search these results, look at them in 3D and download them from\r\nPython or the command line, with no GPU and no docking of your own.\r\n\r\n    pip install -U pocketvina\r\n\r\nDocumentation: https://bioinformatics.mdc-berlin.de/PocketVina/atlas.html\r\nAtlas database: https://bimsbstatic.mdc-berlin.de/akalin/asarigun/pocketvina_atlas/\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- `pocketvina.Atlas`: search proteins and drugs, show their information, list the best scores of a protein or a drug,\r\n  select a protein–drug pair, view it in 3D, run PoseBusters checks, save the poses, and download part of the Atlas\r\n  for offline use\r\n- The `pocketvina atlas` command: `search`, `show`, `export` and `download`\r\n- A new documentation page for the Atlas, with an interactive example\r\n- Examples: `example/atlas.py` and a Colab notebook\r\n  ([open in Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/github/BIMSBbioinfo/PocketVina/blob/main/notebooks/atlas_colab.ipynb)),\r\n  no GPU needed\r\n- The benchmarks page moved out of the documentation; see\r\n  [benchmark/README.md](https://github.com/BIMSBbioinfo/PocketVina/blob/main/benchmark/README.md)\r\n",
