        "body": "PocketVina 0.2.0 adds a new results format, faster runs, and tools to inspect and check the results.\r\n\r\n    pip install pocketvina\r\n\r\nDocumentation: https://bioinformatics.mdc-berlin.de/PocketVina/\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- Results format: Parquet tables and one compact pose file per protein. A stopped run resumes where it stopped.\r\n- Faster runs: seeded ligand preparation, faster receptor conversion, and several engines sharing one GPU.\r\n- New methods: `best_scores()`, `select()`, `show()` (interactive 3D page), `bust()` (PoseBusters) and `export()`.\r\n- Command line: `pocketvina dock`, `info`, `query`, `export`, `show`, `bust`, `setup` and `bench`.\r\n- Documentation, a Google Colab notebook and a conda recipe.\r\n\r\nResults of 0.1 remain usable: `pocketvina import-legacy` converts an old output folder, and `ligand_prep=\"legacy\"`\r\nreproduces the ligand preparation of the published runs.",
